Q: Find the Maximum Value in a Vector Array using Recursion A: <p>Please clearly specify what function accepts and what is should return.
From one perspective it looks like it should return a maximum value and accepts vector and starting index, from other it returns index and accepts vector and starting index.</p>
<p>After specifying this, you should start by writing unit tests (for example):</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>TEST_CASE(&quot;maxVal&quot;) {
    auto [v, expected] = GENERATE(table&lt;std::vector&lt;int&gt;, int&gt;({
        { { 0 }, 0 },
        { { 1 }, 1 },
        { { 2, 1 }, 2 },
        { { 1, 2 }, 2 },
        { { 1, 2, 3 }, 3 },
        { { 5, 2, 3 }, 5 },
        { { 1, 5, 3 }, 5 },
    }));
    CAPTURE(v);
    REQUIRE(maxVal(v) == expected);
}
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://godbolt.org/z/1eoxWYPbK" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://godbolt.org/z/1eoxWYPbK</a></p>
<p>Use warnings as errors to catch some code issues.</p>
<p>When you will have UT then please explain what this should do:</p>
<pre><code>return (maxVal(arr, i + 1) &gt; arr[i]);
</code></pre>
